{
  "_comment": [
    "WRITTEN-DOWN ANSWERS FROM api.github.com'S GIT TREES ENDPOINT, for the three refs this defect is about.",
    "",
    "WHY THE TREES ENDPOINT AND NOT A CONTENTS LISTING. Round 2 of the independent review measured two bypasses",
    "of the contents form: a listing reports a blob's object id, which does not move when only the file MODE does",
    "(so `chmod +x .github/workflows/verifier-receipt.yml` is admitted), and it carries no statement of whether",
    "the page was truncated, so a short page is indistinguishable from a directory that does not hold the entry.",
    "A trees response carries per-entry `mode` and an explicit `truncated` boolean. Nothing here is inferred from",
    "a length.",
    "",
    "EVERY VALUE IS CROSS-CHECKABLE OFFLINE: each entry's `sha` and `mode` are what `git ls-tree <ref> <path>`",
    "reports in the repository's own object store, so a reviewer with no network can confirm the recording is",
    "observed rather than composed. The merge bases likewise equal `git merge-base` for each pair.",
    "",
    "SHAPE. Each tree route is the response body with the fields this module does not read (`url` per entry and",
    "per response, `size` on blobs) dropped; the array is named `tree` and the flag `truncated`, which is what",
    "the endpoint names them. A recording that named the array something else would be a recording of an",
    "endpoint that does not exist - the module reads `tree`, and so does api.github.com.",
    "",
    "TAKEN: 2026-09-23, BAWES-Universe/studenthub-platform, at",
    "  authority 9f0131a5df8687deccd1ac0c0b0dc08f9a3a689b  (the commit the receipt authority landed in)",
    "  base      a51c8490dfb8572917049b3ab73dcf94409365c4  (authority's parent; the merge base for both pairs)",
    "  candidate 6feac016e3a0796d0c7b21d86426af0f1491a9c1  (the candidate run 35852850002 refused, wrongly)"
  ],
